From a143cadab2afd82eb17c8b4aecf565f9ae792247 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Enrico Bartky <enrico.bartky@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 12 Aug 2026 17:15:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] test: retire the Repro scratch tests and the legacy solution
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Batch 2b of the root repository's test-suite retirement item.

ReproTests and ReproT were debugging leftovers. Neither contained a single
assertion: ReproT printed six regex probes to the console, and ReproTests
appended its results to a hard-coded D:\Broiler.JS\repro-out.txt, which on Linux
is treated as a relative filename, so it silently created a file with a colon
and backslashes in its name and passed.

ReproT's probes are already covered — Issue725Tests and Issue723Tests both
assert that an unmatched optional group comes back undefined from exec — so it
is deleted outright.

ReproTests was probing something real that nothing else covers: super property
lookup inside a class *field initializer*, directly under eval, through an arrow
inside eval, and through an arrow declared in one eval statement and invoked in
the next. Issue814DerivedConstructorEvalSuperTests covers the neighbouring
derived-constructor case, which is a different binding — there is no super
constructor call here, only lookup through the field initializer's home object.
Those probes are now ClassFieldInitializerEvalSuperTests, six asserting tests,
all passing. The engine already behaves correctly on every one; until now a
regression in any of them would have been invisible.

BroilerJS.sln is deleted. It could not restore — it referenced Broiler.Regex
paths that moved to Broiler.Regex/ — and Broiler.JS.slnx supersedes it.

The standalone JIntPerfTests executable goes with it. Its eleven scenarios are
exactly the [Params] list of JIntSmokeBenchmarks, which globs the same
OtherTests/JIntPerfTests/Scripts directory from the benchmark project. The
corpus itself is kept and untouched; only Program.cs and the csproj are removed.

Deleting the solution left Broiler.JavaScript.Network and
Broiler.JavaScript.NodePollyfill in no solution. They are deliberately not added
to Broiler.JS.slnx, because neither compiles: both still open
Broiler.JavaScript.Core, a namespace the engine refactor removed, so every file
in them fails CS0234. They were only reachable through a solution that could not
restore, so nothing regressed. Reviving them means repairing the namespace
first; deleting the sources is a separate decision and is not made here. This is
recorded in the status document along with the corrected test counts.

